IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cpp-core-calendar`
IMPORT `cpp-core-age`

-- Tests for cpp-core-age.l4 (section 2(2)). Every expected value is worked out by hand.

§ `Tests of section 2(2)`

§§ `The actual birthday`

-- Born 15 March 1966: sixty years on is 15 March 2026.
#ASSERT `the date a person actually reaches a specified age` (YearMonthDay 1966 3 15) 60 EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2026 3 15)
-- Born 29 February 1964: sixty years on is 29 February 2024, a leap day.
#ASSERT `the date a person actually reaches a specified age` (YearMonthDay 1964 2 29) 60 EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2024 2 29)
-- Sixty-one years on there is no 29 February, so the birthday is 28 February 2025 (assumed clamp, fork F2).
#ASSERT `the date a person actually reaches a specified age` (YearMonthDay 1964 2 29) 61 EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2025 2 28)

§§ `The actual age on a date`

-- The day before the sixtieth birthday the person is 59.
#ASSERT `the actual age of a person in whole years on a date` (YearMonthDay 1966 3 15) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 14) EQUALS 59
-- On the birthday the person is 60.
#ASSERT `the actual age of a person in whole years on a date` (YearMonthDay 1966 3 15) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 15) EQUALS 60
-- A year on, one day short of the sixty-first birthday the person is still 60; on it, 61.
#ASSERT `the actual age of a person in whole years on a date` (YearMonthDay 1966 3 15) (YearMonthDay 2027 3 14) EQUALS 60
#ASSERT `the actual age of a person in whole years on a date` (YearMonthDay 1966 3 15) (YearMonthDay 2027 3 15) EQUALS 61
-- Born 29 February 2000, on 28 February 2025 the person is 25 (assumed clamp, fork F2).
#ASSERT `the actual age of a person in whole years on a date` (YearMonthDay 2000 2 29) (YearMonthDay 2025 2 28) EQUALS 25
-- The day before that, 27 February 2025, the person is still 24.
#ASSERT `the actual age of a person in whole years on a date` (YearMonthDay 2000 2 29) (YearMonthDay 2025 2 27) EQUALS 24

§§ `The deemed date: the first day of the month after the month of the birthday`

-- Sixty on 15 March 2026 is deemed reached on 1 April 2026.
#ASSERT `s 2(2) — the date a person is deemed to reach a specified age` (YearMonthDay 1966 3 15) 60 EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2026 4 1)
-- Sixty on the first day of a month is still deemed reached on the first day of the NEXT month: 1 March 2026 gives 1 April 2026.
#ASSERT `s 2(2) — the date a person is deemed to reach a specified age` (YearMonthDay 1966 3 1) 60 EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2026 4 1)
-- Sixty on the last day of a month: 31 March 2026 gives 1 April 2026.
#ASSERT `s 2(2) — the date a person is deemed to reach a specified age` (YearMonthDay 1966 3 31) 60 EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2026 4 1)
-- Sixty-five on 1 December 2025 is deemed reached on 1 January 2026, across the year end.
#ASSERT `s 2(2) — the date a person is deemed to reach a specified age` (YearMonthDay 1960 12 1) 65 EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1)
-- Born 29 February 1964, sixty on 29 February 2024 is deemed reached on 1 March 2024.
#ASSERT `s 2(2) — the date a person is deemed to reach a specified age` (YearMonthDay 1964 2 29) 60 EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2024 3 1)

§§ `The ten provisions where the actual birthday governs`

-- Paragraph 44(3)(a) is on the list: the date is the actual birthday, 15 March 2026, not 1 April.
#ASSERT `s 2(2) — the date a person is treated as reaching a specified age for a provision` `paragraph 44(3)(a)` (YearMonthDay 1966 3 15) 60 EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2026 3 15)
-- Section 70 is on the list.
#ASSERT `s 2(2) — the date a person is treated as reaching a specified age for a provision` `section 70` (YearMonthDay 1966 3 15) 65 EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2031 3 15)
-- Subparagraph 72(a)(iii) is on the list.
#ASSERT `s 2(2) — the date a person is treated as reaching a specified age for a provision` `subparagraph 72(a)(iii)` (YearMonthDay 1966 3 15) 65 EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2031 3 15)
-- Paragraphs 13(1)(c), 13(1)(e) and 13(1.2)(c) are on the list.
#ASSERT `s 2(2) — the date a person is treated as reaching a specified age for a provision` `paragraph 13(1)(c)` (YearMonthDay 2000 7 20) 18 EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2018 7 20)
#ASSERT `s 2(2) — the date a person is treated as reaching a specified age for a provision` `paragraph 13(1)(e)` (YearMonthDay 2000 7 20) 18 EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2018 7 20)
#ASSERT `s 2(2) — the date a person is treated as reaching a specified age for a provision` `paragraph 13(1.2)(c)` (YearMonthDay 2000 7 20) 18 EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2018 7 20)
-- Paragraphs 17(c), 17.1(c), 19(c) and 19(d) are on the list.
#ASSERT `s 2(2) — the date a person is treated as reaching a specified age for a provision` `paragraph 17(c)` (YearMonthDay 2000 7 20) 18 EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2018 7 20)
#ASSERT `s 2(2) — the date a person is treated as reaching a specified age for a provision` `paragraph 17.1(c)` (YearMonthDay 2000 7 20) 18 EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2018 7 20)
#ASSERT `s 2(2) — the date a person is treated as reaching a specified age for a provision` `paragraph 19(c)` (YearMonthDay 2000 7 20) 18 EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2018 7 20)
#ASSERT `s 2(2) — the date a person is treated as reaching a specified age for a provision` `paragraph 19(d)` (YearMonthDay 2000 7 20) 18 EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2018 7 20)
-- Any provision not on the list takes the deemed date, 1 August 2018.
#ASSERT `s 2(2) — the date a person is treated as reaching a specified age for a provision` `any other provision` (YearMonthDay 2000 7 20) 18 EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2018 8 1)

§§ `Whether the person has reached the age on a date`

-- Deemed: on 31 March 2026 the person born 15 March 1966 has not reached sixty for an ordinary provision.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 2(2) — the person is treated as having reached a specified age on a date for a provision` `any other provision` (YearMonthDay 1966 3 15) 60 (YearMonthDay 2026 3 31))
-- Deemed: on 1 April 2026 the person has.
#ASSERT `s 2(2) — the person is treated as having reached a specified age on a date for a provision` `any other provision` (YearMonthDay 1966 3 15) 60 (YearMonthDay 2026 4 1)
-- Actual birthday governs section 70: on 15 March 2026 the person has reached it, on 14 March 2026 not.
#ASSERT `s 2(2) — the person is treated as having reached a specified age on a date for a provision` `section 70` (YearMonthDay 1966 3 15) 60 (YearMonthDay 2026 3 15)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 2(2) — the person is treated as having reached a specified age on a date for a provision` `section 70` (YearMonthDay 1966 3 15) 60 (YearMonthDay 2026 3 14))

§§ `Periods of months ending or commencing with the age`

-- Sixty on 15 March 2026. (a) a period ending with that time includes March 2026, the month of the birthday.
#ASSERT `s 2(2)(a) — a month is counted in a period of months ending with a specified age` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) (YearMonthDay 1966 3 15) 60
-- (a) includes the months before March, and any day inside the month.
#ASSERT `s 2(2)(a) — a month is counted in a period of months ending with a specified age` (YearMonthDay 2026 2 10) (YearMonthDay 1966 3 15) 60
-- (a) does not include April 2026, the month after.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 2(2)(a) — a month is counted in a period of months ending with a specified age` (YearMonthDay 2026 4 1) (YearMonthDay 1966 3 15) 60)
-- (b) a period commencing with that time does NOT include March 2026.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 2(2)(b) — a month is counted in a period of months commencing with a specified age` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 20) (YearMonthDay 1966 3 15) 60)
-- (b) starts with April 2026.
#ASSERT `s 2(2)(b) — a month is counted in a period of months commencing with a specified age` (YearMonthDay 2026 4 1) (YearMonthDay 1966 3 15) 60
-- (b) a December birthday: the period commencing with age 65 on 1 December 2025 starts January 2026, not December 2025.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 2(2)(b) — a month is counted in a period of months commencing with a specified age` (YearMonthDay 2025 12 1) (YearMonthDay 1960 12 1) 65)
#ASSERT `s 2(2)(b) — a month is counted in a period of months commencing with a specified age` (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) (YearMonthDay 1960 12 1) 65
